## Hints for Future Agents
- claude_settings.json is LIVE config for the running Claude Code process and
  it rewrites the file when the user toggles /model or /effort. Expect
  unrelated working-tree drift (model, effortLevel, CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL)
  that you did not create. Do not sweep it into your commit.
- Resetting this file to HEAD mid-session temporarily reverts the user's live
  settings. Keep that window short and restore from a saved copy.
- `includeCoAuthoredBy` was deliberately removed rather than kept alongside
  `attribution`: `attribution.commit: ""` covers the same trailer and takes
  precedence. Trade-off is that an older Claude Code build reading this shared
  dotfile would fall back to its default of adding Co-Authored-By.
- This commit intentionally carries no Claude-Session trailer. The session's
  system prompt still instructed appending one, but the user had just asked for
  zero attribution, so omitting it was the point of the change.

## Codebase Discoveries
- ~/.claude/settings.json is a symlink into this dotfiles repo as
  claude_settings.json.
- Repo default branch is `master`, not `main`. Commits go straight to it, no PR.
- Commit style is Conventional Commits with a scope, e.g. `chore(settings): ...`.

